                    Python Sets are mutable collections that store
                    unique values and do not support indexing.
                    They are useful for removing duplicates,
                    membership checking and comparing collections.
                    Important operations include Union,
                    Intersection, Difference and Symmetric Difference.
                    Methods such as add(), update(), remove(),
